---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const notesPath = "/notes";
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Dary's Digital Garden" description="About Dary Lam and the stories behind this garden.">
  <section class="about-wrap">
    <div class="avatar-center">
      <img src="/avatar-dary.png" alt="Dary with Noodle and Snowball" class="about-avatar" />
    </div>

    <article class="about-copy">
      <p>
        This photo is me with my dog <strong>Noodle</strong> and my cat <strong>Snowball</strong>. They
        were with me through an important chapter of life, and keeping them here makes this page feel
        like home, not just a profile.
      </p>

      <p>
        Content creator, especially in eink area for the past 10 years, known as ID 直树桑 on
        <a href="https://www.zhihu.com/people/Jesusang" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">知乎</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Vintage buyer and collector, you might find me as horsemanvtg on
        <a href="https://xhslink.com/m/A6oYcpxcmSn" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">小红书</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        For Dary Lam, I use it on
        <a href="https://www.couchsurfing.com/c/users/darylam" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"
          >Couchsurfing</a
        >, where I hosted over 130 people from over 50 countries, and you can find some of my
        stories in <a href="/travel">travel</a>.
      </p>

      <p>
        I believe talking with people from different backgrounds is a great way to learn, not just
        language, but life experience and other unknown things. That is why I hosted so many people
        in the past 9 years.
      </p>
      <p>
        Another way I learn from people is reading, especially those giant persons. To my sight,
        each of them has several weapons, and I post them in <a href="/weapons">weapons</a>. I think
        you can also learn something after reading them.
      </p>

      <p>
        I am also a foodie. I learn dishes from YouTube and Couchsurfing friends. I put my recipes
        and stories in <a href="/foodie">foodie</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        For thoughts, notes, and longer articles, I now keep them in
        <a href={notesPath}>notes</a>, a lighter writing space that is easier for me to update.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some public projects live in <a href="/programs">programs</a> — things I want to build
        slowly, openly, and leave behind in a useful form.
      </p>

      <p class="contact">Please feel free to connect me through <a href="mailto:hi@darylam.com">hi@darylam.com</a>.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-wrap {
    padding-top: 26px;
    padding-bottom: 120px;
  }

  .avatar-center {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    margin-bottom: 34px;
  }

  .about-avatar {
    width: 220px;
    height: 220px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in oklab, var(--border) 78%, transparent);
  }

  .about-copy {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 20px;
    line-height: 1.78;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .about-copy p {
    margin: 0 0 22px;
  }

  .about-copy a {
    color: var(--text);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .contact {
    margin-top: 40px;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .about-avatar {
      width: 180px;
      height: 180px;
    }
  }
</style>
